<h1>Control and Button</h1>

<p>
    Controls attached to the map. The styling here is all on this page &mdash; the library ships no
    CSS for controls and picks no class names.
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Reset</strong> is an action button. It has no state and just does something.</li>
    <li>
        <strong>Show/hide the marker</strong> is a toggle. It reports its state through
        <code>data-visible</code>, which the CSS on this page styles, and swaps its tooltip.
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>Layer</strong> starts disabled and enables itself after two seconds, standing in for
        data that has to load first. While it's disabled it's styled to look absent &mdash; click it
        anyway and nothing happens, which is the point.
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>Zoom in</strong> (the + icon) is an icon-only button. It has no text to be its name,
        so its tooltip is also written to <code>aria-label</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>Satellite</strong> (the globe icon) is an icon-only toggle that shows the word
        &ldquo;Satellite&rdquo; while it's on. While it's off the tooltip is its <code>aria-label</code>.
        Once it has text, the <code>aria-label</code> comes off so the name is the text you can see.
    </li>
    <li><strong>The legend</strong> is a plain <code>Control</code> wrapping markup already on the page.</li>
    <li>
        <strong>Move the legend</strong> and <strong>Remove the legend</strong> show the parts
        <code>addCustomControl()</code> can't do on its own.
    </li>
</ul>

<div style="margin: 10px 0">
    <button id="moveLegend" type="button">Move the legend</button>
    <button id="removeLegend" type="button">Remove the legend</button>
    <button id="addLegend" type="button">Add the legend back</button>
</div>

<p id="status" aria-live="polite" style="margin: 10px 0">&nbsp;</p>

<div id="map" class="mapContainer"></div>

<h2>What each button is called</h2>

<p>
    Updated as the buttons change. A button's name is what a screen reader reads and what a voice
    control user says to press it. The tooltip always goes in <code>title</code>. It only goes in
    <code>aria-label</code>, which would replace the visible text as the name, when the button has
    no text you can see. The text inside each icon's <code>svg</code> doesn't count.
</p>

<table class="TestNames">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th scope="col">Button</th>
            <th scope="col">Visible text</th>
            <th scope="col"><code>title</code></th>
            <th scope="col"><code>aria-label</code></th>
            <th scope="col">Name</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody id="buttonNames"></tbody>
</table>

{# The legend starts here on the page and is moved onto the map by the Control, the way a
   server-rendered legend would be. #}
<div id="legend" class="TestLegend" hidden>
    <p class="TestLegend-title">Legend</p>
    <p class="TestLegend-item">A marker you can hide</p>
</div>

